## Authority model

The ontology is the sole authority. The automation manifest, Jira payloads, agent bundles, workflow, runtime state, and receipts are projections or observations. Never repair a generated artifact by hand. Change the graph and regenerate.

Every external mutation follows:

```text
admitted graph
→ deterministic plan
→ intent receipt
→ explicit apply boundary
→ external response
→ result receipt
→ independent receipt verification
```

Plan-only commands never require tracker or agent credentials.

## Standard lifecycle

```bash
ggen sync run
bash scripts/gall/gall automation validate
bash scripts/gall/gall work status
bash scripts/gall/gall work next
bash scripts/gall/gall work dispatch-ready
```

After implementation work produces its declared evidence:

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall work advance
bash scripts/gall/gall tracker plan
bash scripts/gall/gall receipt verify
```

To run checkpoint evidence and test total closure:

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall checkpoint run
ggen sync run
bash scripts/gall/gall crown
```

## External tracker actuation

External tracker mutation is refused unless the profile is `apply-allowed` and the operator explicitly runs:

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall tracker apply
```

### Jira Cloud environment

```text
JIRA_BASE_URL=https://your-domain.atlassian.net
JIRA_EMAIL=operator@example.com
JIRA_API_TOKEN=secret
JIRA_DEPENDENCY_LINK_TYPE=Blocks
GALL_JIRA_USE_COMPONENTS=0
GALL_JIRA_STATUS_MAP={"blocked":"Blocked","ready":"To Do","complete":"Done"}
```

`GALL_JIRA_STATUS_MAP` is optional because Jira workflow transition names are deployment-specific.

### GitHub Issues environment

```text
GITHUB_TOKEN=secret
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=owner/repository
```

The synchronizer provisions its deterministic labels before upserting issues and closes an issue only after its Gall completion receipt exists.

## Coding-agent actuation

Handoff bundles are always available:

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall work dispatch WORK_ITEM_ID
```

External command-agent invocation additionally requires an `apply-allowed` profile, `command-agent` mode, and:

```text
GALL_AGENT_COMMAND=/path/to/agent-command --fixed-arguments
```

Then execute:

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall work dispatch WORK_ITEM_ID --apply
```

The generated work-order path is appended as the final command argument. Standard output, standard error, intent, and result receipts remain under the generated runtime and receipt directories.

## GitHub Actions automation

The generated `.github/workflows/gall-control-plane.yml` performs plan and replay on pull requests. Manual dispatch can independently request:

- advancement of ready work;
- tracker application;
- one agent handoff or invocation;
- crown verification.

Tracker and agent actuation use the `gall-external-actuation` environment so repository approval rules can guard secrets and execution.

## Refusal conditions

Automation must stop instead of improvising when:

- a dependency is incomplete;
- the work-item DAG is cyclic or violates proof order;
- a context path is missing;
- a write path escapes the repository;
- apply mode is not admitted;
- required credentials are missing;
- a verification command fails;
- an evidence artifact is absent;
- a receipt chain is invalid or stale;
- a checkpoint is not `ALIVE` at crown time.

## Independent replay and receipts

```bash
bash scripts/gall/gall replay
bash scripts/gall/gall receipt verify
```

The receipt verifier recomputes every digest and predecessor link, verifies materialized receipts belong to the chain, and checks the latest receipt against the current generated automation manifest.
